2026-10-27T11:27:52.6091038Z             "body": "## Summary\nRelease the bridge registry lock while ownership renewal and routing I/O run, then revalidate captured selection state before publication. Preserve previous-response continuity policy while rejecting quarantined or retired sessions, stale ownership receipts, and stale routing results. Keep request-owned cancellation teardown and original reservation cleanup outside the registry critical section.\n\n## Scope and provenance\nIndependent topic based directly on main 72630bbfeee9e3b0d9acfb95e2b1e706b8b0188e. Exactly 16 reviewed manifest paths; no deployed composite, CHANGELOG, SOURCE, environment or proof-artifact changes. Frozen manifest SHA-256: f2ab015ed9b4a3ede5379f7b150c12ba19d9991e37105e5ddb1e836bd13f1f9e. Independent Astra/high review ReviewBridgeEligibilityContractR2 reported no actionable findings; all manifest checksums were confirmed before commit.\n\n## Validation evidence\nRetained owning evidence reviewed: 1385 tests passed (232 integration, 89 lifecycle-unit, 1064 proxy-unit); strict specs 67 passed, zero failed. Previous-response quarantine and retirement controls failed before repair and passed afterward; eligible churn and alias-retarget controls passed. No tests were rerun during publication.\n\n## Explicit limits\nOriginal incident causality and recovery remain unknown. Cancellation coverage uses actual SQLite transactions; real PostgreSQL-driver teardown latency and separate owner-read cancellation are not proved. Current-head CI, actionable review threads and mergeability remain acceptance gates; publication is not merge approval. No deployment or shared database changes.",
