2026-10-27T11:27:54.4444563Z ##[group]Run # Note: There is currently no way to distinguish between undefined variables and empty strings in GitHub Actions.
2026-10-27T11:27:54.4445097Z [36;1m# Note: There is currently no way to distinguish between undefined variables and empty strings in GitHub Actions.[0m
2026-10-27T11:27:54.4445456Z [36;1m# This limitation affects how we handle default values and empty inputs.[0m
2026-10-27T11:27:54.4445764Z [36;1m# For more information, see: https://github.com/actions/runner/issues/924[0m
2026-10-27T11:27:54.4446120Z [36;1m[0m
2026-10-27T11:27:54.4446327Z [36;1m# The following logic implements the configuration priority described in the README:[0m
2026-10-27T11:27:54.4446565Z [36;1m#[0m
2026-10-27T11:27:54.4446679Z [36;1m# Inputs[0m
2026-10-27T11:27:54.4446809Z [36;1m# Environment Variables[0m
2026-10-27T11:27:54.4446956Z [36;1m# Config File[0m
2026-10-27T11:27:54.4447088Z [36;1m# Defaults[0m
2026-10-27T11:27:54.4447210Z [36;1m#[0m
2026-10-27T11:27:54.4447443Z [36;1m# As noted above defaults are awkward to handle as GitHub Actions will inject those values as the input[0m
2026-10-27T11:27:54.4447814Z [36;1m# if the caller doesn't provide them, thus if the input matches the default we don't set it as we[0m
2026-10-27T11:27:54.4448183Z [36;1m# can't tell the difference.  Plus if we did set it when it was the default value then it could potentially[0m
2026-10-27T11:27:54.4448586Z [36;1m# override an external environment variable, or something in the callers configuration file, which then wouldn't[0m
2026-10-27T11:27:54.4448921Z [36;1m# match the configuration priority that is documented.[0m
2026-10-27T11:27:54.4449119Z [36;1mset_env_var_if_provided() {[0m
2026-10-27T11:27:54.4449272Z [36;1m  local var_name="$1"[0m
2026-10-27T11:27:54.4449419Z [36;1m  local input_value="$2"[0m
2026-10-27T11:27:54.4449575Z [36;1m  local default_value="$3"[0m
2026-10-27T11:27:54.4449718Z [36;1m[0m
2026-10-27T11:27:54.4449889Z [36;1m  if [ -n "$input_value" ] && [ "$input_value" != "$default_value" ]; then[0m
2026-10-27T11:27:54.4450159Z [36;1m    # If action was provided with explicit input by the caller set that[0m
2026-10-27T11:27:54.4450452Z [36;1m    # Use printf %q to safely escape special characters and prevent command injection[0m
2026-10-27T11:27:54.4450750Z [36;1m    printf 'export %s=%q\n' "$var_name" "$input_value" >> trivy_envs.txt[0m
2026-10-27T11:27:54.4450955Z [36;1m  fi[0m
2026-10-27T11:27:54.4451066Z [36;1m}[0m
2026-10-27T11:27:54.4451177Z [36;1m[0m
2026-10-27T11:27:54.4451344Z [36;1m# Set environment variables, handling those with default values[0m
2026-10-27T11:27:54.4451801Z [36;1m# cf. https://aquasecurity.github.io/trivy/latest/docs/configuration/#environment-variables[0m
2026-10-27T11:27:54.4452109Z [36;1mset_env_var_if_provided "TRIVY_INPUT" "$INPUT_INPUT" ""[0m
2026-10-27T11:27:54.4452473Z [36;1mset_env_var_if_provided "TRIVY_EXIT_CODE" "$INPUT_EXIT_CODE" ""[0m
2026-10-27T11:27:54.4452750Z [36;1mset_env_var_if_provided "TRIVY_IGNORE_UNFIXED" "$INPUT_IGNORE_UNFIXED" "false"[0m
