2026-10-27T11:28:20.2884110Z ##[group]Run # Note: There is currently no way to distinguish between undefined variables and empty strings in GitHub Actions.
2026-10-27T11:28:20.2884891Z [36;1m# Note: There is currently no way to distinguish between undefined variables and empty strings in GitHub Actions.[0m
2026-10-27T11:28:20.2885513Z [36;1m# This limitation affects how we handle default values and empty inputs.[0m
2026-10-27T11:28:20.2886023Z [36;1m# For more information, see: https://github.com/actions/runner/issues/924[0m
2026-10-27T11:28:20.2886392Z [36;1m[0m
2026-10-27T11:28:20.2886729Z [36;1m# The following logic implements the configuration priority described in the README:[0m
2026-10-27T11:28:20.2887130Z [36;1m#[0m
2026-10-27T11:28:20.2887320Z [36;1m# Inputs[0m
2026-10-27T11:28:20.2887532Z [36;1m# Environment Variables[0m
2026-10-27T11:28:20.2887779Z [36;1m# Config File[0m
2026-10-27T11:28:20.2887992Z [36;1m# Defaults[0m
2026-10-27T11:28:20.2888193Z [36;1m#[0m
2026-10-27T11:28:20.2888583Z [36;1m# As noted above defaults are awkward to handle as GitHub Actions will inject those values as the input[0m
2026-10-27T11:28:20.2889213Z [36;1m# if the caller doesn't provide them, thus if the input matches the default we don't set it as we[0m
2026-10-27T11:28:20.2900815Z [36;1m# can't tell the difference.  Plus if we did set it when it was the default value then it could potentially[0m
2026-10-27T11:28:20.2901540Z [36;1m# override an external environment variable, or something in the callers configuration file, which then wouldn't[0m
2026-10-27T11:28:20.2902216Z [36;1m# match the configuration priority that is documented.[0m
